  "conclusion": "The hidden discrepancy accumulates across decoder layers before final normalization and LM-head projection. The corrected BF16 KV plus BF16 linear-attention convolution-state emulation models the in-place single-token decode update and changes post-MLP final RMSE from 0.1032561 to 0.1028437; it does not remove the drift. Post-token-mixer tracing shows the same gradual accumulation, from layer 0 RMSE 0.0002270 to layer 63 RMSE 0.0885137, while the post-MLP boundary reaches 0.1028437. An independent CUDA Transformers oracle with the same storage emulation matches all greedy tokens but retains nearly identical logit drift, ruling out host-vs-device reference math as the primary cause. No tolerance or acceptance criterion was changed. The next diagnostic boundary is an operation/state comparison at the first affected layer."
